      "worked": "Take $a=-1$, $b=0$ and $c=-1$. These satisfy every printed premise.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta &= b^{2}-4ac\\\\\\Delta &= 0^{2}-4(-1)(-1)\\\\\\Delta &= -4<0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $-x^{2}-1=0$ has no real roots. This counterexample disproves the claim as printed.",
